-- Map sensor dust across a folder; every render heals it first.
--
-- A dust spot lives on the sensor, so it sits at exactly the same
-- place in every frame while the world moves behind it. Detection is
-- therefore a vote, not a vision problem: each frame is divided by
-- its own local blur so lighting cancels, and a dip that survives the
-- median across frames is dust -- a bird or a branch moves, and the
-- median forgets it. No model is asked for anything; a run over a
-- whole shoot costs preview reads and arithmetic.
--
-- The finding is a dust map kept beside the photographs. From then on
-- every render of the folder -- baseline, preset, treatment, or a
-- hand-tuned version -- heals the listed spots before anything else
-- touches the frame. An empty map is a finding too: a clean sensor,
-- on record, so the question is not asked again.

param photos: text = "."
param pattern: text = ""
param edge: num = 768

use python "dust_kernel.py"

-- Every readable frame votes; the map is their agreement.
found := survey_dust(photos, pattern, edge)
check map_valid(found)
print(map_note(found))

-- The map lives beside the photographs, under the house folder,
-- where the renderer already knows to look.
where := map_home(photos)
check map_valid(found)
act file.overwrite(where, found)
settle until check file_exists(where) within 5
commit(found)
